## 7. Entity lifecycle callbacks on the Owner entity

**None.** There are no `@PrePersist`, `@PostPersist`, `@PreUpdate`, `@PostLoad`, or any other JPA lifecycle callbacks anywhere in `src/main/java` (grep returned no matches), including in `Owner.java`, `Person.java`, and `BaseEntity.java`. The `Owner` entity has `@Transient` derived getters (`getMembershipLevel` lines 175-185, `getIdentityKey` lines 194-200) and a `@Transient sharesHousehold` field (lines 87-88), but no callback hooks — all default-setting is done explicitly in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` before `ownerRepository.save`.

`BaseEntity.isNew()` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java`, lines 44-47) returns `id == null`; the id is `@GeneratedValue(strategy = IDENTITY)` (lines 33-35), so `isNew()` drives every `owner.isNew()` branch in `saveOwner`.

